# QuantiumV regression test list.
# Columns (| separated, no | inside a field): tag | testbench | extra
# files (comma-separated, may be empty) | cwd (design or testbench) |
# cores (comma-separated subset of fsm,ref,pipe) | expect (pass, or
# xfail:<reason>) | timeout seconds (blank = script default) | extra
# iverilog flags (optional, e.g. -P parameter overrides).
# Blank lines and #-comments ignored.
#
# "cores" tracks which of the three core builds (see run_regress.sh
# --core) this test is meaningful for at this point in the pipelining
# track -- see the plan at C:\Users\Potato\.claude\plans\
# research-the-c-extension-reflective-candle.md. run_regress.sh --core
# X actually SKIPS any row not listing X (wired up as part of P3.3,
# which is also when the "ref" value first became real). "pipe" rows
# get added as design/pipe/ comes online (P4a onward), per the
# ARCH/RET/STIM/UARCH test-class breakdown in that plan. At the P4a
# gate: core_pipe's own module tests plus every core-level test whose
# program stays within what core_pipe implements. The rest need loads/
# stores, FENCE, A, M divide, U/S modes, interrupts, debug or Sv39, or
# are white-box tests reading core.sv internals (state, fstate, TLB
# registers) that get a QV_PIPE_AS_CORE variant when their feature lands.
#
# 8 rows stay fsm-only: the design/*_tb.sv unit tests that instantiate
# a leaf module (alu/c_expand/csr_file/divider/register_file) directly
# by its fixed FSM name -- verification/reference/'s ref_* counterparts
# have no such name alias (unlike ref_core.sv, which answers to `core`
# under -DQV_REF_AS_CORE), so these simply don't have a ref-side
# equivalent to run.

# === design/*_tb.sv ===
design_alu_tb|design/alu_tb.sv||design|fsm|pass|
